1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,242
When you get
a deep cut,

2
00:00:01,242 --> 00:00:02,876
a doctor weaves
a curved surgical

3
00:00:02,876 --> 00:00:04,696
needle through both
edges of your skin—

4
00:00:05,250 --> 00:00:06,593
pulling the thread
tight like

5
00:00:06,593 --> 00:00:08,034
a zipper to lock
the wound shut,

6
00:00:08,034 --> 00:00:09,404
then snipping
the ends clean.

7
00:00:10,250 --> 00:00:12,120
Inside, the skin
turns red and inflamed

8
00:00:12,120 --> 00:00:13,423
as millions
of repair cells

9
00:00:13,423 --> 00:00:14,868
rush in to rebuild
the damage.

10
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:16,905
Next, golden
collagen fibers weave

11
00:00:16,905 --> 00:00:18,724
across the gap like
living scaffolding,

12
00:00:18,724 --> 00:00:19,874
spinning brand
new skin!

13
00:00:20,450 --> 00:00:21,530
Tiny new blood vessels

14
00:00:21,530 --> 00:00:22,724
branch through
the seam,

15
00:00:22,724 --> 00:00:24,827
pumping oxygen to nourish
the fresh tissue—

16
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:26,289
and a few
weeks later,

17
00:00:26,289 --> 00:00:27,604
the stitches
slide right out—

18
00:00:27,604 --> 00:00:29,419
leaving your skin
healed back together!
